.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "December 2025" "Simple Shell Manual"

.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command line interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell
.br
.B echo "command" | simple_shell

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a basic UNIX command interpreter that reads commands from standard input or from a file and executes them. It is designed as a simplified version of the traditional sh shell.

The shell operates in two modes:
.TP
.B Interactive mode
Displays a prompt and waits for the user to type a command.
.TP
.B Non-interactive mode
Reads commands from standard input without displaying a prompt.

.SH INVOCATION
In interactive mode, the shell displays the prompt
.B "($) "
and waits for user input. Commands are executed after pressing Enter.

In non-interactive mode, commands can be piped to the shell:
.br
.B echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh

.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
The shell locates commands in the following order:
.TP
1.
Built-in commands (exit, env)
.TP
2.
Absolute paths (/bin/ls)
.TP
3.
Relative paths (./program)
.TP
4.
Commands found in PATH directories

.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell with the last command's exit status.
.br
Usage: exit
.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment variables.
.br
Usage: env

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive mode:
.nf
@Username ➜ /workspaces/holbertonschool-simple_shell (dev) $ ./hsh 
($) ls /var
backups  cache  lib  local  lock  log  mail  opt  run  spool  tmp  vscode-remote
($) echo holberton
holberton
($) exit
@Username ➜ /workspaces/holbertonschool-simple_shell (dev) $
.fi

.TP
Non-interactive mode:
.nf
@Username ➜ /workspaces/holbertonschool-simple_shell (dev) $ ./hsh 
($) /bin/ls /var | hsh

backups  cache  lib  local  lock  log  mail  opt  run  spool  tmp  vscode-remote
($) exit
@Username ➜ /workspaces/holbertonschool-simple_shell (dev) $
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
The shell returns the exit status of the last executed command.
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution
.TP
.B 127
Command not found
.TP
.B 126
Command found but not executable

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATH
Colon-separated list of directories to search for commands.
.TP
.B All environment variables
Accessible through the
.B env
built-in command.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The shell returns the exit status of the last command executed. If no command was executed, it returns 0.

